  "method": "Optimized Rust WASM, same 256-byte UTF-8 input/output ABI and JS bridge for both engines. Exact outputs checked against forced temporal-polyfill basic on every input. 1,024 warmup calls, nine rotating samples per engine, 8,192 calls per sample. Encoding, parsing, operation, output formatting/decoding and checksum included. Native Rust APIs measured separately. Invalid-input controls run for both WASM engines.",
  "scope": "Instant parsing/rounding/serialization and Duration parsing/serialization only. No calendar/timezone data or JS Temporal class facade. FormatJS WASM uses no_std and buffer formatting; temporal_rs wrapper uses std allocator, public Writeable output for Instant, public String formatting for Duration. Minimal Rust WASM sizes are not full polyfill or full backend sizes. TS module exports additional primitive operations; basic reference includes eight classes. No cold-start performance claim.",
